{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Trip to Japan**\n\nJapan, a land where tradition and modernity dance harmoniously, left me enchanted during my recent visit. From the neon-lit streets of Tokyo to the serene temples of Kyoto, every moment was a discovery.\n\nI arrived in Tokyo, a city pulsating with energy. Skyscrapers like the Shibuya Sky offered breathtaking views, while the tranquil Meiji Shrine provided a stark contrast. The culinary adventure began at Tsukiji Outer Market, where fresh sushi and delicate wagashi (traditional sweets) tantalized my taste buds.\n\nA bullet train whisked me to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Wandering through Fushimi Inari’s torii gates and Kinkaku-ji’s golden pavilion felt like stepping into a painting. The geisha district of Gion, with its wooden machiya houses, exuded timeless elegance.\n\nNara, with its friendly deer and Todai-ji Temple, was another highlight. The gentle giants bowed for treats, adding a touch of whimsy to the historic setting.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without a soak in an onsen. Hakone’s mineral-rich waters, surrounded by misty mountains, melted away my travel fatigue.\n\nFrom the precision of a tea ceremony to the chaos of Osaka’s Dotonbori street food, Japan surprises at every turn. My suitcase laden with matcha treats and souvenirs, I left with a promise to return—this time, to explore the snowy north or the subtropical islands.\n\nJapan isn’t just a destination; it’s an experience that lingers long after the journey ends.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.053566593676805496}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.07330837845802307}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.429121196269989}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -3.1470757676288486e-05}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.7633236050605774}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.020777663215994835}, {"token": " Japan", 